      },
      "body": "My main concern is that this masks the accounting problem rather than fixing it.\nIf the collision invalidates a mempool-sourced transaction after an unrelated extra transaction has been counted, `extra_count > 0`, so the guard still subtracts that unrelated credit.\nI've reimplemented it in https://github.com/l0rinc/bitcoin/pull/229, which fails with `[0 != 1]` against this implementation.\n\nCould we track the source of each slot and decrement `extra_count` only when the invalidated transaction came from `extra_txn`?",
      "created_at": "2026-07-15T20:55:21Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-15T20:55:34Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35727#discussion_r3590685127",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
